message.content:
{
  "classifications": [
    {
      "document_id": "993",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "Although the senators announce a concrete funding award and praise its congressional approval, the release does not state that they authored the legislation, requested the funds, or otherwise caused the award. This aligns with the negative example for Rule 1."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "4608",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The senators sent a letter pushing for solutions and asking the Secretary to address financial constraints. This constitutes a request that has not produced an attributed result, which the codebook explicitly states is not credit-claiming."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "2795",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "1"
      ],
      "explanation": "The release explicitly states that Senator Murray \"has secured 80 million in funding\" and \"secured the funding in the Senate Commerce Justice and Science CJS Appropriations bill.\" This is a direct claim of attributing a concrete funding award to the senator's own efforts."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3391",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "Senator Domenici hosted a conference, sought input, and expressed his opinions on the need for water reforms. The document describes policy views and meetings without attributing any concrete legislative action, funding, or program to the senator's specific efforts."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "2052",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "This is a brief announcement regarding the availability of a teleconference recording where the senator answered reporters' questions. It does not claim any legislative leadership or responsibility for a concrete outcome."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3400",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The senator is denouncing and criticizing the President's decision to commute a prison sentence. The codebook states that mere criticism and policy opinions are not credit-claiming."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "1806",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "1"
      ],
      "explanation": "The release claims that Senators Clinton and Schumer (along with other delegation members) \"fought hard to save\" the funds, \"helped lead the effort to save the 9/11 responder funds,\" and \"secured the commitment of House Speaker Dennis Hastert to include the 125 million.\" This explicitly attributes a concrete funding outcome to their efforts."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3522",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The senators are urging President Bush to secure an international climate agreement and help poorer nations. This is a policy demand or request that has not yet produced an attributed result."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3552",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "This text is a statement expressing the senator's views on a modified amendment and thanking other senators for their work. Although he briefly refers to \"our bill\" as a point of policy comparison regarding criminals, the text primarily functions as policy opinion and commentary on another member's amendment, rather than claiming a leading legislative role or concrete result."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "2473",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "Senator Schumer sent a letter demanding to know an ambassador nominee's position and criticizing official US policy. This is a request and a policy criticism that has not produced an attributed outcome."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "classifications": [
    {
      "document_id": "3492",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "2"
      ],
      "explanation": "The release explicitly states that Senator Dodd is the \"author of the landmark Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA)\" and announces that he \"will introduce\" new legislation to provide paid leave, thereby claiming a leading legislative role in authoring and introducing legislation."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "1620",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The senator announces placing a hold on an EPA nominee to demand a technical analysis. This is an announcement of an action but it does not claim authorship of legislation or that a concrete governmental outcome or benefit has been secured."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3274",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "1"
      ],
      "explanation": "The senator explicitly claims credit for securing federal funding, stating \"we have appropriated over $6 billion\" and \"Senator Specter and I have worked to fund efforts to prepare against SARS, severe acute respiratory syndrome, bioterrorism and smallpox.\""
    },
    {
      "document_id": "396",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "1"
      ],
      "explanation": "The press release quotes a state official directly attributing federal funding for ferry security improvements to Senator Murray's efforts (\"the support that Patty and others have been able to bring from the federal government for this is very welcome\"), thus claiming credit for a concrete funding outcome."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "1185",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "2"
      ],
      "explanation": "Senator Pryor claims a leading legislative role by announcing that \"his legislation to help prevent children from drowning in pools has passed the Senate,\" clearly asserting responsibility for advancing the legislation."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "4746",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "Senator Hutchison merely announces the passage of a bill into law. She does not claim to have introduced, sponsored, authored, or secured passage of the bill herself (the release notes it was introduced by Senator Inhofe), making this an announcement without a claimed senatorial role in causing the outcome."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "4575",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "2"
      ],
      "explanation": "The document notes that Senator Sununu \"has consistently supported elimination of the death tax, having co-sponsored legislation to do so\" and is an \"original co-sponsor of the Jobs Protection and Estate Tax Reform Act of 2005,\" which constitutes claiming a leading legislative role (sponsorship)."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3118",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "Senator Kerry's statement on the State of the Union Address consists of policy opinions and criticisms of the administration. He does not claim credit for any concrete outcomes, benefits, or leading legislative roles."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "878",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "Senator Lugar announces that the City of Columbus was awarded HUD funding, but the press release only states he was \"notified\" of the grant and does not attribute the outcome to his own efforts. This matches the codebook's negative example for rule 1."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "2544",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "2"
      ],
      "explanation": "The document explicitly highlights Senator Kennedy's leading legislative role, describing him as the \"chief author\" and \"a lead author of the Leave No Child Behind Act.\""
    }
  ]
}

{
  "classifications": [
    {
      "document_id": "926",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The senators urge the President to approve a request for federal disaster assistance, but the text does not state that the request has been approved or that the assistance has been obtained. Under the codebook, requests that have not produced an attributed result are not credit-claiming."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "2085",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "1",
        "2"
      ],
      "explanation": "The senator claims credit for a concrete outcome by stating he \"lobbied the U.S. Department of Labor to approve the application\" for worker retraining assistance (Rule 1). Additionally, the text notes he \"helped craft the program\" and \"spearheaded the most comprehensive expansion and overhaul of the TAA program,\" claiming a leading legislative role (Rule 2)."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "417",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "2"
      ],
      "explanation": "The senator claims a leading legislative role by stating he \"helped introduce legislation\" to provide disaster assistance and that the new bill \"incorporates provisions from legislation Baucus previously introduced.\" This clearly falls under Rule 2 for introducing and authoring legislation."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3837",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "2"
      ],
      "explanation": "The press release identifies Senator Bennett as one of the \"authors of four major pieces of healthcare legislation now making the rounds in Congress,\" specifically co-authoring the Healthy Americans Act. This satisfies Rule 2 regarding claiming authorship of legislation."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "1722",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "2"
      ],
      "explanation": "The senators claim a leading legislative role by stating they are \"offering\" the Prevention First amendment today and that they previously \"introduced S 20 the Prevention First Act,\" satisfying Rule 2 for authoring and introducing legislation."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "1363",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The text discusses the senator's vote to move forward on a bill and his policy arguments against the estate tax. Explaining a vote and expressing policy opinions do not constitute credit-claiming according to the codebook, as he does not claim authorship, sponsorship, or that he secured a concrete outcome."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "1942",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The senator is described as pressing public health experts for recommendations, suggesting that local governments set up registries, asking questions, and chairing a committee hearing. He does not claim to have secured a concrete governmental benefit or to have authored/sponsored legislation, so this is not credit-claiming."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3377",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "1"
      ],
      "explanation": "The senator announces a concrete federal grant and connects it to her own efforts by highlighting that she is on the specific Appropriations Subcommittee that funds the program and \"fights each year to increase its federal funding.\" By doing so, she presents herself as instrumental in advancing the funding outcome for the program that provided the grant (Rule 1)."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "59",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The senator expresses strong policy opinions, criticizes the administration's budget proposals, and vows to \"stand up and fight these bad policies.\" While the text mentions she \"consistently fought for legislation to punish companies,\" she does not claim authorship, sponsorship, or securing passage of a specific bill, nor does she claim to have delivered a concrete outcome. Thus, these are mere policy opinions and criticisms."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "32",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "2"
      ],
      "explanation": "Although the senator merely announces a new veterans' clinic and an ethanol plant without claiming to have secured them, he explicitly claims a leading legislative role later in the text by stating, \"I have introduced the Cellulosic Ethanol Incentive Act.\" This satisfies Rule 2."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "classifications": [
    {
      "document_id": "1587",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "2"
      ],
      "explanation": "The press release highlights Senator Enzi receiving an award for \"his efforts to help pass legislation\" and explicitly states he \"worked to pass legislation this Congress to enhance drug safety.\" This constitutes a claim of actively advancing legislation and having a leading legislative role."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3335",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "1"
      ],
      "explanation": "Senator Biden claims that he actively advanced the ratification process to open the Holocaust archives by detailing his advocacy, letters to ambassadors, and continued pressure on non-ratifying countries, thereby presenting his efforts as instrumental in achieving the final governmental outcome."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "1901",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "2"
      ],
      "explanation": "Senator Collins explicitly claims she \"coauthored\" provisions in the Heroes at Home Act and \"authored\" a provision requiring a DoD study, successfully adding these measures to the Defense Authorization bill passed by the Senate."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "2953",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "2"
      ],
      "explanation": "Senator McConnell announces that he \"reintroduced Kids First,\" demonstrating a claim of introducing, sponsoring, and taking a leading legislative role in the health care legislation."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "953",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "Senator Cochran merely expresses approval and praises Mayor Brown regarding her appointment to the Farm Service Agency state committee. He does not claim that he was responsible for or instrumental in securing her appointment."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "4449",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "Senator Tester's statement is purely a ceremonial memorial honoring the victims and first responders of September 11. The codebook explicitly excludes ceremonial statements from being classified as credit-claiming."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "2955",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "Senator Domenici announces a defense contract awarded to Honeywell Inc. but does not state that he secured it, requested it, or otherwise caused the award, which aligns perfectly with the negative example for Rule 1."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "4466",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "1"
      ],
      "explanation": "Senator Coleman states, \"We have worked hard at the federal level to ensure that assistance is available,\" attributing the availability of federal disaster assistance for his constituents directly to these efforts."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "927",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "2"
      ],
      "explanation": "Senators Schumer and Clinton announce that the \"Schumer Clinton amendment\" has been included in the final report of the Fiscal Year 2006 Foreign Operations Appropriations Bill, claiming authorship and the successful addition of an amendment to legislation."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3408",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "Senator Sununu announces USDA funding for a local water system but attributes the result to the Department of Agriculture's commitment, without claiming any senatorial role in securing or obtaining the grant. This matches the negative example for Rule 1."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "classifications": [
    {
      "document_id": "518",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "2"
      ],
      "explanation": "Senator Lieberman claims sponsorship of various budget amendments (e.g., \"These amendments sponsored by Lieberman,\" \"co-sponsored by Senator Lieberman\"). This fits the rule for claiming a leading legislative role, including sponsoring legislation."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "955",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "1"
      ],
      "explanation": "The press release states that the USDA \"accepted the request on behalf of the Massachusetts delegation to provide assistance,\" successfully connecting the delegation's letter to the concrete governmental outcome of receiving emergency assistance."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3267",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "2"
      ],
      "explanation": "The document notes that Senator Byrd reached an agreement on the comprehensive Senate mine safety bill and explicitly lists him as one of the sponsors, matching the rule for claiming a leading legislative role."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3051",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The senator simply states his vote in support of renewing the Voting Rights Act. As the negative example for Rule 2 explains, a statement explaining a vote does not claim authorship, sponsorship, or responsibility for advancing legislation."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "1847",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "This is a ceremonial statement mourning the passing of Pope John Paul II. Ceremonial statements are explicitly excluded from credit-claiming in the codebook's definition."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3852",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The press release features policy opinions, criticism of Republican budgets, and advocacy for LIHEAP funding. It does not attribute any concrete governmental outcome or legislative success to the senator's own efforts."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "962",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "Senator Clinton calls for the federal government to cover long-term medical monitoring, which constitutes a request that has not yet produced an attributed result. Thus, it is not credit-claiming."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3142",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "1"
      ],
      "explanation": "The press release highlights that Chamber members thanked Senator Lugar for \"his help in bringing two Air National Guard missions to the Hulman Regional Airport,\" attributing a concrete governmental outcome to the senator's efforts."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "1885",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "1",
        "2"
      ],
      "explanation": "The senator claims credit both for successfully adding her amendment to the NDAA (Rule 2) and for playing a \"key role\" in removing the Niagara Falls Air Reserve Station from the base closure list in 2005 (Rule 1)."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "2013",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The senators announce and applaud a concrete federal grant from the Department of Homeland Security, but the text does not say they secured it, requested it, or otherwise caused the award, directly matching the negative example for Rule 1."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "classifications": [
    {
      "document_id": "3303",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The senator is announcing that he sent an open letter requesting the President to take action regarding sanctions on Sudan. This is a request that has not produced an attributed result, and therefore does not constitute credit-claiming."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "1952",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The senator is expressing policy opinions and questioning nominees during a committee hearing. She is not claiming responsibility for a concrete outcome or a leading legislative role."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3199",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The senator is making a ceremonial statement by presenting an award to a housing development. There is no claim that she secured funding, authored legislation, or otherwise caused a concrete governmental outcome."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3859",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The senator announces a federal grant award for local fire departments but does not claim to have secured the funds. While she notes that she \"strongly supported the creation of the FIRE Act Grant program,\" supporting or voting for a program is a policy position and does not rise to the level of authorship, sponsorship, or securing a concrete outcome."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3291",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The senator announces the award of federal funds to a local fire department but does not attribute the receipt of these funds to his own efforts. He simply states his ongoing commitment to working in Congress."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "2168",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "2"
      ],
      "explanation": "The senator explicitly claims a leading legislative role by stating she \"joined Sens. Ted Stevens (R-AK) and Daniel Inouye (D-HI) in introducing the Call Home Act of 2006.\""
    },
    {
      "document_id": "2176",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The senator is announcing a series of federal grant awards from the Department of Homeland Security but does not claim any personal role or effort in securing or delivering the funds."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "1931",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The senator is sharing her perspective on a corporate merger and providing the text of a letter she wrote expressing her concerns. She is stating a policy opinion and making a request, not claiming credit for a concrete governmental outcome or legislative action."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "2964",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The senator's office announces a federal grant from the Department of Health and Human Services but does not attribute the funding award to the senator's own efforts."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "4791",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The senator announces federal grant awards and notes that he serves on the subcommittee which sets funding for such programs. While this implies a connection, it stops short of explicitly attributing the concrete funding award to his own efforts, such as claiming he actively secured the funds."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "classifications": [
    {
      "document_id": "1223",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "2"
      ],
      "explanation": "Senator Conrad claims a leading legislative role by stating that he worked closely to forge the bipartisan 2002 Farm Bill, a piece of enacted legislation."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "4411",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "1",
        "2"
      ],
      "explanation": "Senator Burns claims credit for introducing S. 2315, thereby claiming a leading legislative role (Rule 2). He also attributes a concrete governmental funding outcome to his own efforts by stating he restored over $900 million for Byrne/JAG funding in an amendment to the Budget Resolution (Rule 1)."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "1315",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The senators claim credit for pressuring a private company (BP) to stop plans to dump more pollution into Lake Michigan. However, the codebook limits credit-claiming to \"governmental\" benefits, policies, programs, funding outcomes, or legislative action. Pressuring a private corporation to change its internal business practices does not meet this strict criterion."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "4287",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "1"
      ],
      "explanation": "The senators attribute a concrete benefit—a $400,000 contract for a local firm—to their own efforts, stating that they helped connect the company with large contractors and federal agencies as part of their effort to spur economic development."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "707",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The senator merely provides a statement of opinion on a judicial outcome (a jury verdict). There is no claim of responsibility for the verdict, nor any mention of a legislative role or governmental benefit secured by his efforts."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "2071",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The release announces that the senator delivered a radio address and discussed a policy issue. There is no claim of securing a concrete governmental outcome or leading a legislative effort."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "2866",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "2"
      ],
      "explanation": "Senator Feinstein explicitly claims a leading legislative role by stating she \"authored legislation in the 109th Congress\" to criminalize border tunnels, and notes that the bill language was included in an appropriations bill and signed into law."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3504",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The senator details his ongoing efforts, meetings, and the placement of a 'hold' on a nominee to secure future commitments from the Department of Interior. Because these efforts and requests have not yet produced a concrete, attributed result, they do not constitute credit-claiming under the provided rules."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "777",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The senator is giving a speech to advocate for the passage of legislation granting retroactive immunity. He argues for his policy position but does not claim authorship, sponsorship, or responsibility for advancing the bill, nor does he claim to have delivered a concrete governmental outcome."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "2212",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "2"
      ],
      "explanation": "The release explicitly states that Senator Domenici authored the bill and that Senator Bingaman cosponsored it. Claiming authorship and sponsorship of legislation, especially a bill that has been signed into law, is a clear claim of a leading legislative role."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "classifications": [
    {
      "document_id": "428",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "Rule 2"
      ],
      "explanation": "Senator Leahy explicitly claims a leading legislative role by stating, \"Six years ago I introduced a bill to limit mergers...\" and \"When I introduced this bill...\" This constitutes a claim of introducing legislation under Rule 2, making the document credit-claiming."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3137",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "Rule 1"
      ],
      "explanation": "While Senator Schumer announces the grants, the document goes beyond a simple announcement by claiming that \"Schumer Has Pushed For Additional Funding\" and that he \"was among the first senators who recognized the need for the federal government to establish a funding program...\" By claiming he pushed for the funding and helped establish the program, he attributes the broader governmental program and funding outcomes to his own efforts and advocacy."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "2347",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The document is an announcement of the Senate's legislative schedule and an explanation of Senator Frist's policy position on the gun liability legislation. It does not contain any claims that Frist authored, introduced, or successfully secured passage of the legislation or that he delivered a concrete governmental outcome."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3174",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "Senator Roberts merely announces a concrete grant awarded by the Office of National Drug Control Policy. The text does not claim that he requested, secured, or otherwise caused the grant to be awarded, fitting exactly the negative example for Rule 1."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "1087",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "Rule 1"
      ],
      "explanation": "Senators Snowe and Collins explicitly state, \"The funding we worked to secure in the Commerce Justice and Science Appropriations bill...\" This directly attributes the concrete funding awards to their own efforts, fulfilling Rule 1."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "765",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "Rule 1",
        "Rule 2"
      ],
      "explanation": "Senator Leahy claims he and a bipartisan coalition \"introduced legislation\" and \"unveiled the Guard and Reserve Readiness and Retention Act\" (Rule 2). He also claims credit for a concrete governmental benefit by noting that he \"successfully worked to make uninsured members of the Guard and Reserves eligible for TRICARE\" (Rule 1)."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "948",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "Rule 2"
      ],
      "explanation": "Senator Cantwell claims a leading legislative role regarding the Media Ownership Act by explicitly stating, \"I was an original cosponsor of the Act.\" Sponsoring legislation is a direct trigger for credit-claiming under Rule 2."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "1304",
      "label": "1",
      "codebook_rule": [
        "Rule 2"
      ],
      "explanation": "The release announces that \"a group of bipartisan senators introduced the Women's Retirement Security Act of 2007 today\" and explicitly lists the senators who cosponsored the legislation. Claiming introduction and sponsorship of a bill qualifies as credit-claiming under Rule 2."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "2284",
      "label": "0",
      "codebook_rule": [],
      "explanation": "The text consists of Senator Kerry's criticism of the White House and his policy opinions regarding Medicare and health care costs. It does not claim any authorship of legislation or attribution of a concrete governmental outcome to his own efforts."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "504",
      "label": "0",
